test LPS in psp8 format, symmetry=on

Reference convergence (2026-10-28)
----------------------------------
The former SCF charge threshold left solver-dependent energy differences
larger than the existing 1e-7 eV acceptance tolerance. Only scf_thr is
tightened to 1e-11. The structure, pseudopotential, plane-wave cutoff,
band count, k-point settings, mixing, default CG solver and iteration
budgets remain unchanged. No comparison tolerance is relaxed.

Independent MPI4 calculations at scf_thr=1e-11:

  cg    -55.79955807013258 eV
  dav   -55.79955807013874 eV
  ppcg  -55.79955807012987 eV

All three SCF calculations converged; their energy span is 8.868e-12 eV.
Tightening CG once more to scf_thr=1e-12 changes its energy by 5.706e-12
eV, also below the original tolerance. The two stored energy fields come
from the independent 1e-11 CG run; other reference fields are unchanged.

Validation used GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10 and CPU Release, with one
OpenMP/OpenBLAS/MKL thread. Executable SHA-256:
bdf544c3e792c5ce7ea973e32ab093dffa563c09ce76956fbbfcf582d1a5eecf.
To reproduce, start each solver from a clean copy of this case, set
ks_solver to cg, dav or ppcg, and run the original Autotest.sh with
-n4 -o1. Repeat CG with scf_thr=1e-12 to check threshold stability.
